From 16eb0df35dd50ceeb7d54fbdc2b477259005b111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tanzeel Khan <140405735+tanscorpio7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:41:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build with newer GCC, glibc, OpenSSL and CMake (#5035)

Babelfish failed to build on current toolchains (GCC 15/16, glibc 2.43+,
OpenSSL 4, CMake 4, e.g. Ubuntu 26.04). The extensions compile with
-Werror, so every warning a newer compiler adds breaks the build, and
regular CI pins ubuntu-22.04 / GCC 11, so none of this was caught.

Engine PR  https://github.com/babelfish-for-postgresql/postgresql_modified_for_babelfish/pull/807

Task: BABEL-7211

Author: Tanzeel Khan <tzlkhan@amazon.com>
